 ## Verified Facts
 
-- `TripViewBeta` reserves a 35px status action row below its right-side data grid. Pending trips expose Iniciar Viaje and Cancelar Viaje; in-progress trips expose Completar Viaje and Cancelar Viaje; terminal states expose neither. `ConfirmTripStatusUpdate` gathers the typed transition, a trimmed comment (required for cancellation), and `ChangeTripStatusMedia` grouped by fiscal merchandise item ID. Its source uses the existing unregistered `.asset` image-upload/camera pipeline, correlates each completion to a row/event, keeps the first completed image as avatar, and blocks confirmation until pending uploads/camera requests finish or are cancelled. Removal aborts local uploads and ignores late responses. Before presentation/submission, asset merchandise requires unique linked store/warehouse/subaccount origin and destination snapshots; media requires unique trip-merchandise IDs and safe image basenames. The server remains authoritative for actual asset state and tenant records. The beta `changeStatus` method submits the trip ID, requested status, comment and media through the typed wrapper. Status actions are disabled while the request is pending. Only a successful API response changes the local trip/status and calls the parent status callback; a guarded getTrip refresh loads the new status/comment notes, while failed requests retain the prior status. Responses from a changed session are ignored, while successful responses still notify the parent if the detail was closed. These facts were verified in source; browser/upload behavior remains unverified because the package build is blocked by dependency resolution.
+- `TripViewBeta` reserves a 35px status action row below its right-side data grid. Pending trips expose Iniciar Viaje and Cancelar Viaje; in-progress trips expose Completar Viaje and Cancelar Viaje; terminal states expose neither. Start/complete actions use the shared green crystal modifier and cancel uses red, with matching hover/focus accents and a dimmed disabled state. `ConfirmTripStatusUpdate` gathers the typed transition, a trimmed comment (required for cancellation), and `ChangeTripStatusMedia` grouped by fiscal merchandise item ID. Its source uses the existing unregistered `.asset` image-upload/camera pipeline, correlates each completion to a row/event, keeps the first completed image as avatar, and blocks confirmation until pending uploads/camera requests finish or are cancelled. Removal aborts local uploads and ignores late responses. Before presentation/submission, asset merchandise requires unique linked store/warehouse/subaccount origin and destination snapshots; media requires unique trip-merchandise IDs and safe image basenames. The server remains authoritative for actual asset state and tenant records. The beta `changeStatus` method submits the trip ID, requested status, comment and media through the typed wrapper. Status actions are disabled while the request is pending. Only a successful API response changes the local trip/status and calls the parent status callback; a guarded getTrip refresh loads the new status/comment notes, while failed requests retain the prior status. Responses from a changed session are ignored, while successful responses still notify the parent if the detail was closed. These facts were verified in source; browser/upload behavior remains unverified because the package build is blocked by dependency resolution.
 - `MediaViewer` honors `currentView` with a zero-index fallback, presents clickable `thump_` thumbnails and previous/next navigation for multiple files, and uses the selected file for downloads/rotations/deletion. Direct image source assignment avoids an older image-load callback replacing a newer selection. Each `MediaFile` can supply its own URL base; `allowsMediaActions: false` hides mutation/download actions for staged evidence while existing callers retain the default behavior.
 - `Sources/App/App.swift` is the `@main` app entry point.
 - The app registers `./service.js` during launch.
